# This file intentionally sets no npm options for `npm install`/`npm ci` on
# CI (GitHub Actions) or Vercel — lifecycle scripts run normally there.
#
# Note for local development on the SCNU project sandbox machine: that
# environment's user-level ~/.npmrc enforces `allow-scripts=@anthropic-ai/claude-code`,
# which makes project-scoped `npm install` fail with EALLOWSCRIPTS for any
# dependency not explicitly allowlisted. The fix lives in that machine's
# user-level ~/.npmrc (`ignore-scripts=true`), NOT in this file, so the
# workaround stays local and does not silently disable postinstall scripts
# for other contributors, CI, or production builds. If you hit EALLOWSCRIPTS
# locally, add `ignore-scripts=true` to your own user-level npmrc instead of
# committing it here.
